    "turn_idx": 9,
    "turn_text": "I think it does merit study, Jim, but I would tell you, I would approach the idea of expanding remote voting with a great deal of skepticism. Part of accountability in government is being in the place where the voting is happening to be accessible to the public and also to colleagues in the legislature. And remote voting on an embarrassing mistake in the way this bill was thrown together is terrible, but you know it's just a one off and I guess we can live with it. We have no choice. But the idea that this would become a fixture of legislative process is really concerning and we would if anybody begins talking about that we should you know we the BGA of course will carefully study both sides of the issue but my gut tells me it's a really bad idea because it moves against the whole notion of open and accountable government.",
